    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nTreat dictation and command mode as two consumers of the same scene registry, with an independent active selection for each role.\r\n\r\n- add `scenes.active_command_scene`, defaulting and falling back to `__command__`\r\n- route each command recording through the command scene selected when that session starts\r\n- expose both roles in the CLI and GUI: `scene use-dictation` (`scene use` remains an alias), `scene use-command`, role markers, and separate selection actions\r\n- provide configurable runtime switchers for dictation (`Shift_R`) and command mode (`F9`); identical bindings can toggle between the two menus\r\n- prevent removal of a scene while it is active for either role\r\n- update English and Chinese UI strings and documentation\r\n\r\nA scene may serve either role or both. Command mode still supplies selected text and the spoken instruction to the chosen scene; this unifies scene configuration and selection, not the two modes' input semantics.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\nCurrently, users cannot easily switch between different LLMs for command mode because it is pinned to the built-in `__command__` scene. Scenes already hold the shared LLM post-processing configuration\u2014prompt, provider, model, candidate count, timeout, and context\u2014but command configuration remains a special case, preventing users from selecting or switching reusable scene configurations independently of ordinary dictation.\r\n\r\nUsing the existing scene model avoids introducing a separate command hierarchy while allowing command mode to choose a different provider or model from dictation.\r\n\r\n## Compatibility\r\n\r\nExisting configurations without `active_command_scene` continue to use `__command__`. The existing `active_scene` field, `vinput scene use` command, and saved dictation-menu bindings remain supported.\r\n\r\n## Automated validation\r\n\r\n- clean release build\r\n- all 3 CTest targets passed\r\n- project lint and documentation build passed\r\n\r\nThis is a relatively large cross-layer change, so feedback and comments on the design, scope, and implementation are very welcome.\r\n\r\n## Manual validation\r\n\r\nVerified locally:\r\n\r\n- GUI **Use for Dictation** and **Use for Command** actions assign independent scenes and display the corresponding badges.\r\n- The `F9` switcher changes only the command scene, and command recording uses the newly selected scene.\r\n- The `Shift_R` switcher changes only the dictation scene.\r\n- `vinput scene list` reports the expected independent **DICTATION** and **COMMAND** markers.\r\n- Dictation and command selections persist after restarting Fcitx5 and `vinput-daemon`.\r\n- `vinput scene use-command <id>`, the GUI, and the `F9` switcher remain synchronized.",
